X6100 IU1WXY firmware: terms of use

Copyright (c) 2026 Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY. All rights reserved.

1. What this covers

These terms cover the X6100 IU1WXY firmware: the radio interface program, its
scripts and data written by Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY ("the IU1WXY software").
They apply from version 0.128. In the source, the IU1WXY software is every
file with the notice "SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-IU1WXY-Terms", and
every other file of the firmware that has no licence notice of its own and is
not part of the software listed in section 6.

The firmware image also contains software by other authors under their own
licences (see section 6). Those licences are not changed by these terms.

2. What you may do

- Install and use the firmware, free of charge, on Xiegu X6100 radios you own or use.
- Make copies of the image for that purpose and keep backups.
- Pass the unmodified image to other X6100 owners, free of charge, with these terms.

3. What you may not do

- Sell the firmware, or include it in a product or service you sell, without
  written permission.
- Modify, decompile or disassemble the IU1WXY software, or publish works derived
  from it, except where section 6 or the law allows it.
- Remove or change the copyright notices, the name or the credits.
- Present the IU1WXY software, or parts of it, as your own work.
- Reproduce the screens of the IU1WXY software, as set out in section 4.

4. Screens and visual design

The screens of the IU1WXY software are part of the IU1WXY software and are
covered by its copyright: their layout, menus, icons, themes, colours,
graphics, the arrangement of text and the way information is shown on them.

Without written permission you may not reproduce, copy or imitate them, in
whole or in a recognisable part, in other firmware, software, apps, websites,
devices or any other product or material. This applies however it is done:
by copying the code, by redrawing them, by recreating them from screenshots,
photos or videos, or with any other tool.

You may still take and share screenshots, photos and videos of the firmware
running on a radio, to show it, review it, teach it or report a problem,
as long as it is clear that they show the X6100 IU1WXY firmware.

5. No warranty

The firmware is provided "as is", without any warranty. You use it at your own
risk. IU1WXY is not liable for damage to the radio, to other equipment, or for
any other loss arising from its use. Transmitting is your responsibility under
your licence.

6. Other software in the image

The image contains software under open licences. The main parts:

| Software | Licence | Your rights |
|---|---|---|
| Linux kernel 6.1.82 with the X6100 patches and configuration, rtl8723bu WiFi driver with our patches, BusyBox 1.36.1, U-Boot 2023.01 and the other GPL-2.0 system packages | GPL-2.0 (some GPL-2.0+) | full source at the address below |
| x6100-js8d (JS8 modem, on js8core by Jordan Sherer KN4CRD and the JS8Call contributors), x6100-jttyd (JTTY, from WSJT-X by K1JT and the WSJT-X team), x6100-wsprd (WSPR decoder by K1JT and K9AN, via rtlsdr-wsprd by VA2GKA): separate programs | GPL-3.0 | full source at the address below |
| Bash, readline, less, nano, parted, dosfstools, gsl and the other GPL-3.0 system packages | GPL-3.0+ | full source at the address below |
| aether-x6100-control (radio control library, Georgy Dyuldin), glibc, PulseAudio, GLib, BlueZ libraries, libnm, ALSA, libsndfile, FFmpeg and the other LGPL libraries | LGPL-2.1+ (some LGPL-3.0+) | linked as shared libraries: you may replace them with modified versions and reverse engineer the parts needed to debug such changes; source at the address below |
| GPL-3.0 modem source incorporated in the radio interface program and built into its separate helper programs: src/js8 with third-party/js8core (JS8, on the JS8Call engine by Jordan Sherer KN4CRD and contributors; also x6100-js8d), src/wspr (WSPR decoder by K1JT and K9AN; also x6100-wsprd), src/jtty (JTTY from WSJT-X by K1JT and the WSJT-X team; built into x6100-jttyd) | GPL-3.0 | full source at the address below |
| LVGL 8.3 (gdyuldin fork), lv_drivers, ft8_lib (Karlis Goba), liquid-dsp (Joseph Gaeddert), cJSON (Dave Gamble), cty.dat (Jim Reisert AD1C), mp4-muxer, siimple-icons, bottle, bottle-sqlite, and other MIT/X11 system packages | MIT | notices in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES |
| PFFFT (Julien Pommier, Hayati Ayguen, Dario Mambro), CRC++ (Daniel Bahr), speex, opus, libvorbis, OpenSSH, wpa_supplicant and the other BSD packages | BSD | notices in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES |
| Eigen (in js8core) | MPL-2.0 | source at the address below |
| Fonts: DejaVu (Bitstream Vera licence), Roboto (Apache-2.0), Share Tech and Share Tech Mono (Carrois Type Design, SIL OFL 1.1), Font Awesome Free icons (SIL OFL 1.1) | as listed | licence texts in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES |
| EiBi shortwave schedule (Eike Bierwirth) | free use and distribution | see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES |
| Realtek WiFi and Bluetooth firmware (linux-firmware) | redistributable binary | see the package licence |

The PSK31/PSK63, Olivia, Bluetooth-device, audio-resampler (olivia_resamp) and
LVGL display-driver configuration files of the radio interface program are
IU1WXY's own code under the terms above, not third-party software. Only the
GPL-3.0 modem source listed in the table (JS8, WSPR, JTTY) and the libraries
and system packages above are by other authors.

The complete list of packages in the image, each with its version and licence,
and the full licence texts are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, installed on the radio
in /usr/share/x6100/licenses/ together with these terms and the licence files
of every package (/usr/share/x6100/licenses/packages/).

Address of the source code: the Releases page of
https://github.com/IU1WXY/X6100-IU1WXY (file
X6100-IU1WXY-v<version>-gpl-sources.tar.gz). It holds, for each version, the
source of the GPL and LGPL parts listed above with our patches and build
files, the kernel configuration and the list of upstream source archives
used. The same source can also be requested at info@x6100-link.it.

Nothing in these terms limits the rights those licences give you for that
software.

7. Data sent to x6100-link.it

What the radio sends and why is described in the privacy notice at
https://x6100-link.it/privacy.php.

